{"schema_version":"1.0.0","id":"cik-0002019505","cik":"0002019505","slug":"health-in-tech-019505","name":"Health In Tech, Inc.","ticker":"HIT","exchanges":["Nasdaq"],"sector":"Insurance Agents, Brokers & Service","sic":"6411","country":"FL","website":"","listed_years":1.4,"first_annual":"2025-03-17","last_filing":"2026-07-30","annual_only":false,"edgar_url":"https://www.sec.gov/cgi-bin/browse-edgar?action=getcompany&CIK=0002019505&type=10-K","summary":{"sentences":["Health In Tech, Inc. files with the SEC under \"Insurance Agents, Brokers & Service\", based in FL, and has been publicly reporting for 1 year.","It reported $34.6m of revenue over the trailing four quarters, up 9.4% against the same quarter a year earlier, at a gross margin of 51.4%.","Listed on Nasdaq, it is still consuming cash, with roughly 36 months of runway at the current burn."],"generated":true,"note":"Assembled from filing metadata and XBRL figures. Not editorial judgement - and rule 7 asks whether *you* can explain it, so rewrite this in your own words before you rely on it."},"bull":[{"text":"Growth has been positive in all 4 year-on-year comparisons, so this is a trend rather than one good quarter.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2019505/000121390026056707/0001213900-26-056707-index.htm","accession":"0001213900-26-056707"},{"text":"Gross margin of 51.4% means most of each additional sale falls through to cover fixed costs.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2019505/000121390026056707/0001213900-26-056707-index.htm","accession":"0001213900-26-056707"},{"text":"Net cash of $10.3m against total assets of $29.0m - no debt overhang forcing decisions.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2019505/000121390026056707/0001213900-26-056707-index.htm","accession":"0001213900-26-056707"},{"text":"Share count is close to flat (0.6% over the year), so growth in the business accrues to existing holders rather than being diluted away.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2019505/000121390026056707/0001213900-26-056707-index.htm","accession":"0001213900-26-056707"}],"bear":[{"text":"Growth is erratic - a standard deviation of 32.3% across 4 comparisons. Lumpy revenue usually means few customers or long contracts, and both make any single quarter a poor guide.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2019505/000121390026056707/0001213900-26-056707-index.htm","accession":"0001213900-26-056707"},{"text":"Gross margin compressed from 66.8% to 51.4% against the same quarter a year earlier. Either input costs are rising or the company is discounting to hold volume.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2019505/000121390026056707/0001213900-26-056707-index.htm","accession":"0001213900-26-056707"},{"text":"About 36 months of cash at the current burn ($10.3m against $3.5m a year). A company that must raise is a company that raises on the buyer's terms.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2019505/000121390026056707/0001213900-26-056707-index.htm","accession":"0001213900-26-056707"},{"text":"Only 7 quarters of reported history. There is no track record here to speak of, and a short series flatters whatever the recent trend happens to be.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/cgi-bin/browse-edgar?action=getcompany&CIK=0002019505"},{"text":"No officer history could be reconstructed from public filings, so the team - the thing that matters most - is the thing we know least about.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/cgi-bin/browse-edgar?action=getcompany&CIK=0002019505"},{"text":"Base rate: 57.8% of US common stocks underperformed one-month Treasury bills over their lifetimes (Bessembinder, Journal of Financial Economics, 2018). Nothing above changes that starting point.","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jfineco.2018.06.004"}],"triggers":[{"id":"gross_margin_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Gross margin falls below 43.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric